# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rust / Cargo
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compiled output for every crate in the workspace (and the wasm frontend,
# which keeps its own `target/`). A bare `target/` matches any directory of
# that name at any depth.
target/

# We are a dependency
Cargo.lock

# Backup files emitted by `rustfmt`.
**/*.rs.bk

# `cargo mutants` writes its report here (`missed.txt`, `outcomes.json`, per-mutant logs). It is
# machine output and a new one is produced by every run; CI uploads it as an artifact instead.
# The *configuration* — `.cargo/mutants.toml` — is committed, because the scope is a decision.
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# MSVC debug symbols.
*.pdb

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Java / Gradle
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compiled output for every module under java/. A bare `build/` matches any directory of that
# name at any depth, mirroring how `target/` is handled for Cargo above.
build/
.gradle/
# The wrapper jar itself IS committed (it's how CI and a fresh clone get the exact pinned
# Gradle version without a local install); only its ad hoc distribution cache is not.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment & secrets (never commit these)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
# Any `*.env` file, wherever it lives. The patterns above match only files *named* `.env…`,
# so a file such as `deploy/local.env` slips past them and is tracked by accident. Match by
# suffix as well, and ship `*.env.example` instead.
*.env
!*.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDE / editor metadata
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent / assistant tooling caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.serena/cache/
.serena/*.local.yml
.junie/tools

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs & OS junk
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# The shared toolchain is its own workspace, so it has its own target directory.
/cli/target/

# ...and, unlike the library above, its lock file is committed. A library resolves against whatever
# a consumer already has, so pinning here would be a claim it cannot keep; `cli/` ships a *binary*,
# and the lock file is what makes a release build reproducible and what cargo-deny and Renovate act
# on.
!/cli/Cargo.lock
!/cli/fuzz/Cargo.lock
